.TH MMRUN 1 "2026-10-12" "MetaMonitor 0.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mmrun \- run a command and publish the progress it prints to MetaMonitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mmrun
[\fB\-n\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-id\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-\-\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs \fICOMMAND\fR on a pseudo-terminal, mirroring its output unchanged,
and parses it for progress: OSC 9;4 sequences, percentages, GRASS
GRASS_INFO_PERCENT, GDAL dotted counters and N/M counters.
The slot ends \fBdone\fR on exit status 0 and \fBfailed\fR otherwise.
The exit status of \fBmmrun\fR is that of \fICOMMAND\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fINAME\fR
Label shown in MetaMonitor (default: the command line).
.TP
.BR \-\-id " " \fIID\fR
Slot identifier (default: command name and pid).
.SH EXAMPLES
mmrun \-n "Sync rasters" \-\- rsync \-a \-\-info=progress2 src/ dst/
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR metamonitor (1),
.BR mmctl (1)
